  "description": "Tests whether a component of the Hubble tension can be represented as an environment-dependent Cepheid clock bias predicted by the Temporal Equivalence Principle. The prespecified primary full-ladder projection yields H0 = 71.771 +/- 0.990 km/s/Mpc (3.94 sigma from Planck); a separate host-level reconstruction yields H0 = 66.65 +/- 1.58 km/s/Mpc (0.45 sigma from Planck).",
